# local model weights, corpora dumps and wheels — 70 GB, pre-staged on the box.
# Never committed: they are inputs to the run, not artifacts of it, and a single
# safetensors shard is larger than GitHub's hard file limit.
gb10/

# macOS finder droppings — one got committed in 3aca041
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# secrets — never commit
.airlock_key
.airlock_resume_token

# Generated corpora and results.
#
# SRS §14 lists these as REQUIRED submission attachments, so they are tracked even
# though they are regenerable — a judge who clones the repo must get the evidence, not
# instructions for rebuilding it:
#   data/benign_v1.jsonl + manifest + ATTRIBUTION.md   python bench/build_benign.py --seed 1337
#   results/fpr_report.json, results/*.png             python bench/report.py
#   results/proof_*.log                                bash stack/proof.sh | tee
#   results/REPORT.md, results/false_positives.md      python bench/report.py
#
# data/sensitive_v1.jsonl is DELIBERATELY NOT tracked, and this is the one exception to
# the rule above. It is 450 records of realistic-looking credentials, and GitHub push
# protection rejects it — GH013, on the synthetic SLACK_BOT_TOKEN and AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
# values at lines 12, 58 and 89. They are fake, but they are convincing enough to trip a
# secret scanner, which is exactly what a PAYMENT_CARD/CREDENTIAL corpus is supposed to
# be. Publishing a file of plausible live keys to teach a detector is a bad trade even
# when the keys are invented, so §14's attachment is the BUILDER plus the manifest and
# the per-class recall table, not the corpus itself:
#   bench/build_sensitive.py + data/sensitive_v1.manifest.json  (seed 1337, reproducible)
#
# Still ignored below: raw dumps, and the pip/venv noise.
data/sensitive_v1.jsonl
data/dumps/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# generated submission build
submission/SUBMISSION.final.md
results/scores_*.json
results/ablation.json
results/ablation/
results/ablation_table.md
results/fpr_raw.json
results/seats.json
results/calibration.json

